WEBVTT

1
00:43:41.986 --> 00:43:45.986
Are there any guests today? Give a wave if you are here for the first time.

2
00:43:46.986 --> 00:43:49.986
Who is here for the first time today, besides the two-handed people?

3
00:43:50.986 --> 00:43:51.986
Give a wave.

4
00:43:52.986 --> 00:43:53.986
No one?

5
00:43:54.986 --> 00:43:56.986
Ah, everyone is just furniture. Great.

6
00:43:57.986 --> 00:43:59.986
Welcome to the church. Hallelujah.

7
00:44:00.986 --> 00:44:02.986
Make some applause for my dear sister Debbie.

8
00:44:05.986 --> 00:44:09.986
Who didn't know she is my sister? Was there anyone who didn't know she is my sister?

9
00:44:09.986 --> 00:44:11.986
Didn't you know she is my sister?

10
00:44:12.986 --> 00:44:14.986
Then you see the same beauty, right?

11
00:44:21.986 --> 00:44:24.986
I get to share something about giving today.

12
00:44:25.986 --> 00:44:29.986
And I will start with the fact that God created the heavens and the earth.

13
00:44:30.986 --> 00:44:35.986
And He has placed a number of laws in the creation.

14
00:44:36.986 --> 00:44:37.986
Regularities.

15
00:44:37.986 --> 00:44:39.986
For example, gravity.

16
00:44:40.986 --> 00:44:43.986
Everyone knows that if you throw a ball up, it comes back down again.

17
00:44:44.986 --> 00:44:45.986
That's logical.

18
00:44:46.986 --> 00:44:49.986
Everyone also knows that if you put a seed in the ground, a plant will come out of it.

19
00:44:50.986 --> 00:44:51.986
And from that plant comes fruit.

20
00:44:52.986 --> 00:44:56.986
And that fruit is always more than that one seed you put in.

21
00:44:57.986 --> 00:44:58.986
That is a law of nature.

22
00:44:58.986 --> 00:44:59.986
That is a law of nature.

23
00:45:00.986 --> 00:45:07.986
But do you also know that this law of sowing and reaping applies to everything in your life?

24
00:45:08.986 --> 00:45:15.986
It is not only about those seeds that you put in the ground, a farmer who sows them and then reaps the harvest from that.

25
00:45:16.986 --> 00:45:19.986
No, it applies to all aspects of our own lives as well.

26
00:45:20.986 --> 00:45:25.986
If you sow a smile in the store, you will get a smile back.

27
00:45:25.986 --> 00:45:34.986
If you sow grumpiness in your home, early in the morning, with your morning mood, then you will also get grumpiness back.

28
00:45:35.986 --> 00:45:37.986
I certainly do not have that.

29
00:45:38.986 --> 00:45:39.986
No, really not.

30
00:45:40.986 --> 00:45:45.986
The Bible even says it. The Bible teaches this as well.

31
00:45:46.986 --> 00:45:50.986
If you sow sin, you will reap death.

32
00:45:50.986 --> 00:45:55.986
If you sow love for God, you will also reap love for God.

33
00:45:56.986 --> 00:46:01.986
Let's take a look at the text that I have chosen. The first one, number 6.

34
00:46:02.986 --> 00:46:09.986
Consider this when you want to give something. A person who sows sparingly will also reap sparingly.

35
00:46:10.986 --> 00:46:18.986
Yes, logically. A farmer with five hectares of land, if he only has one hectare he wants to sow,

36
00:46:18.986 --> 00:46:27.986
in the spring, and he is too lazy to do more, you should not be surprised that he can only harvest one hectare in the autumn as well.

37
00:46:28.986 --> 00:46:33.986
Logical. Whoever sows sparingly will also reap sparingly.

38
00:46:34.986 --> 00:46:36.986
And someone who sows generously will also reap generously.

39
00:46:37.986 --> 00:46:40.986
Here the Bible speaks about giving, about finances.

40
00:46:40.986 --> 00:46:43.986
So it is not only about your actions.

41
00:46:44.986 --> 00:46:51.986
If you are unjust, if you gossip, if you have slander, then you will also reap that.

42
00:46:52.986 --> 00:46:54.986
Reaping something rotten in your life.

43
00:46:55.986 --> 00:46:58.986
If you do good, then you will also reap good things again.

44
00:46:59.986 --> 00:47:04.986
And the Bible even says that this also applies to giving, to your financial aspect.

45
00:47:05.986 --> 00:47:06.986
But it also applies to your time.

46
00:47:06.986 --> 00:47:16.986
If you give your time, I know of a number of people here who have said, I will take time off from my work to be able to cook in the winter kitchen.

47
00:47:17.986 --> 00:47:20.986
And then you might ask, how do you reap that?

48
00:47:21.986 --> 00:47:29.986
Those people have simply reaped back for the whole year, one day a week paid off.

49
00:47:30.986 --> 00:47:33.986
That is a testimony, something you cannot comprehend with your mind.

50
00:47:33.986 --> 00:47:37.986
But God has established that as a law in creation, also for us.

51
00:47:38.986 --> 00:47:40.986
If you sow, you will reap.

52
00:47:41.986 --> 00:47:43.986
And giving, you will also reap from it.

53
00:47:44.986 --> 00:47:46.986
For, let’s look further at what else is said.

54
00:47:48.986 --> 00:47:51.986
Everyone must decide for themselves how much they want to give.

55
00:47:52.986 --> 00:47:54.986
Just like that farmer, he only feels like sowing one hectare.

56
00:47:55.986 --> 00:47:56.986
Yes, he must know for himself.

57
00:47:57.986 --> 00:47:58.986
You may also decide for yourself.

58
00:47:59.986 --> 00:48:00.986
Just pray about it.

59
00:48:00.986 --> 00:48:02.986
And let him give it willingly. If you give something, do it wholeheartedly, do it joyfully.

60
00:48:03.986 --> 00:48:05.986


61
00:48:06.986 --> 00:48:07.986
Without reluctance or compulsion.

62
00:48:08.986 --> 00:48:10.986
God loves people who give with a joyful heart.

63
00:48:11.986 --> 00:48:12.986
Because that is what it is all about.

64
00:48:13.986 --> 00:48:16.986
If you are grumpy, you will also reap grumpiness.

65
00:48:17.986 --> 00:48:19.986
So give joyfully and God will provide again.

66
00:48:20.986 --> 00:48:21.986
For just look at what it says in verse 8.

67
00:48:22.986 --> 00:48:25.986
And God is able to give you everything abundantly.

68
00:48:26.986 --> 00:48:28.986
I found it so beautiful last week, said Ruben.

69
00:48:29.986 --> 00:48:33.986
It does not say here that God will give you a lot of money.

70
00:48:34.986 --> 00:48:36.986
And that is not necessary either.

71
00:48:37.986 --> 00:48:39.986
God will provide in your life.

72
00:48:40.986 --> 00:48:46.986
As a result, you will have more than enough in all things, at every moment.

73
00:48:47.986 --> 00:48:49.986
So it is about providence.

74
00:48:50.986 --> 00:48:52.986
Do you have enough to eat? Do you have a roof over your head?

75
00:48:52.986 --> 00:48:54.986
Do you have clothing?

76
00:48:55.986 --> 00:48:56.986
God provides.

77
00:48:57.986 --> 00:48:59.986
And that is what you will reap.

78
00:49:00.986 --> 00:49:08.986
And then it says, and I find that very beautiful, as a result, you will have more than enough in all things, at every moment.

79
00:49:09.986 --> 00:49:12.986
And as a result, you can also give a lot to others.

80
00:49:13.986 --> 00:49:14.986
How beautiful is that?

81
00:49:14.986 --> 00:49:15.986
How beautiful is that?

82
00:49:16.986 --> 00:49:23.986
That when you sow, financially, when you give to God, He will provide for your life.

83
00:49:24.986 --> 00:49:25.986
Then you will not lack anything.

84
00:49:26.986 --> 00:49:30.986
And I actually want to challenge you, and even the Bible speaks about this.

85
00:49:31.986 --> 00:49:34.986
The Bible literally says, challenge God then.

86
00:49:35.986 --> 00:49:36.986
Try it then.

87
00:49:37.986 --> 00:49:39.986
That if you sow sparingly, you will reap sparingly.

88
00:49:39.986 --> 00:49:48.986
But if you sow generously and with love and full of joy, God will provide in your life.

89
00:49:49.986 --> 00:49:51.986
And I want to challenge you to take that extra step.

90
00:49:52.986 --> 00:49:54.986
Chris and I have been married for 30 years now.

91
00:49:55.986 --> 00:49:58.986
And for 30 years we have decided to give our tenth.

92
00:49:59.986 --> 00:50:01.986
Ten percent. Immediately when the money comes in.

93
00:50:02.986 --> 00:50:03.986
Not at the end of the month, because then it is often gone.

94
00:50:04.986 --> 00:50:06.986
No, immediately at the beginning of the month.

95
00:50:06.986 --> 00:50:09.986
And we have always seen that God has provided.

96
00:50:10.986 --> 00:50:12.986
Not in money, as Ruben said last week.

97
00:50:13.986 --> 00:50:16.986
But in materials, in things, in provision.

98
00:50:17.986 --> 00:50:22.986
When we prayed for a house, the house and everything came at the right time.

99
00:50:23.986 --> 00:50:25.986
God has always provided.

100
00:50:26.986 --> 00:50:30.986
And I actually want to challenge you to that law that He Himself has placed in it.

101
00:50:31.986 --> 00:50:35.986
It is not something I am making up here, but what God Himself has placed in it.

102
00:50:36.986 --> 00:50:37.986
Try that law out for once.

103
00:50:38.986 --> 00:50:41.986
Just try it out and give generously and give me joy.

104
00:50:42.986 --> 00:50:44.986
And God will provide. Amen.

105
00:50:52.986 --> 00:50:53.986
Yes.

106
00:50:54.986 --> 00:50:55.986
Is everyone happy?

107
00:50:57.986 --> 00:50:59.986
The question is whether the Lord is happy.

108
00:51:00.986 --> 00:51:01.986
Amen.

109
00:51:02.986 --> 00:51:04.986
Have you been married for 30 years?

110
00:51:05.986 --> 00:51:07.986
Were you five when you got married?

111
00:51:11.986 --> 00:51:13.986
Scoring points, scoring points.

112
00:51:14.986 --> 00:51:18.986
I sometimes have to go eat biestik, so then I want to score some points.

113
00:51:19.986 --> 00:51:20.986
Hallelujah.

114
00:51:22.986 --> 00:51:24.986
Thank you, Bent. Please have a seat.

115
00:51:25.986 --> 00:51:27.986
Yes, that's fine too.

116
00:51:35.986 --> 00:51:43.986
I think it's good that I give a little recap, a little repetition about last week's teaching.

117
00:51:44.986 --> 00:51:52.986
Because it is a very large piece of teaching that I gave last week and I think it is good.

118
00:51:54.986 --> 00:52:00.986
I realize that the church, especially the Western church, with our Western eyes, with our modern way of reading.

119
00:52:01.986 --> 00:52:08.986
I realize that it is good and healthy for us to learn to read the depths of God's Word.

120
00:52:09.986 --> 00:52:14.986
Also in the mindset and worldview of the people who wrote it.

121
00:52:15.986 --> 00:52:16.986
Do you understand what I mean?

122
00:52:17.986 --> 00:52:28.986
So when you read the Bible, we modern people of today, we read it in a fairly flat way.

123
00:52:29.986 --> 00:52:36.986
And we assume that if a text is written, that text also means what it says.

124
00:52:37.986 --> 00:52:40.986
That is a Western way of reading Scripture.

125
00:52:41.986 --> 00:52:48.986
However, you cannot necessarily impose that on all texts across all times.

126
00:52:49.986 --> 00:52:59.986
Different texts, different times, different cultures, different ways of writing, different meanings of writing, different intentions of writing.

127
00:53:00.986 --> 00:53:05.986
This is important, because I believe that if you want to know the depths of God's Word,

128
00:53:06.986 --> 00:53:11.986
one of the great teachers from whom I have learned a lot once said, the Bible is like a symphony.

129
00:53:12.986 --> 00:53:13.986
It is not one instrument.

130
00:53:13.986 --> 00:53:16.986
It is not just the sung word, even if you look at it flatly.

131
00:53:17.986 --> 00:53:20.986
It is indeed a symphony with many, many layers in it.

132
00:53:21.986 --> 00:53:29.986
And when you start to explore the depths of those layers, you will discover how powerful God's Word is and how impossible it is.

133
00:53:30.986 --> 00:53:36.986
I tell you emphatically, how impossible it is that it could merely be the work of agreed-upon men.

134
00:53:37.986 --> 00:53:46.986
God's Word is so complex, so wonderful, it is so deep, that no one on this earth is smart enough to write that.

135
00:53:47.986 --> 00:53:48.986
And I mean that seriously.

136
00:53:49.986 --> 00:53:56.986
And I am not just talking about what someone writes at a moment, because I really find Paul to be an amazing apostle.

137
00:53:57.986 --> 00:54:06.986
And no one in this room has the philosophical, psychological, spiritual depth of Paul.

138
00:54:07.986 --> 00:54:10.986
What he writes often is truly, how can a human conceive this?

139
00:54:11.986 --> 00:54:13.986
Then only filled with the Holy Spirit, of course.

140
00:54:14.986 --> 00:54:18.986
But then you are talking about one letter from a man at a certain time.

141
00:54:19.986 --> 00:54:22.986
But then the coherence of the whole Scripture.

142
00:54:23.986 --> 00:54:32.986
And there are scholars of the Bible who say that the Bible may have been written over a period of 1500 years in total.

143
00:54:33.986 --> 00:54:36.986
Some say maybe 2000 years, some say maybe longer.

144
00:54:37.986 --> 00:54:41.986
But let's assume for a moment that it was written over a period of 1500 years.

145
00:54:42.986 --> 00:54:44.986
And it still has to be coherent.

146
00:54:45.986 --> 00:54:48.986
And still from people who really do not live in the same place.

147
00:54:48.986 --> 00:54:51.986
One lived here and the other thinking of Europe.

148
00:54:52.986 --> 00:54:55.986
The other lived completely on the other side of the continent.

149
00:54:56.986 --> 00:55:00.986
And what he writes there is coherent with what was written 1500 years ago.

150
00:55:01.986 --> 00:55:03.986
And then you think that it is also a beautiful text.

151
00:55:04.986 --> 00:55:05.986
This is deep.

152
00:55:06.986 --> 00:55:08.986
There has never been anything as beautiful written as the Bible.

153
00:55:09.986 --> 00:55:14.986
Glory to the logos. Amen and amen. Really. Amazing.

154
00:55:15.986 --> 00:55:17.986
And I have a purpose in saying this now.

